course: dictionary
lesson: 14286
title: Notation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Notation is a system of signs or symbols used to write things down. «In maths, 3 × 4 = 12 uses the × sign to show multiply.» The × sign, the = sign and the numbers are all part of the notation.
explain: Notation can also mean one written note or mark. «The teacher added a small notation in the margin.» Here it means a single note, not a whole system of symbols.
explain: Each subject has its own notation. Music uses notes written on a stave, and science uses scientific notation to write very big or very small numbers. Ask yourself: is this a set of symbols, or one written note? The words around it will tell you which.
fact: Notation means a system of signs or symbols used for writing things down.
fact: «Notation» can also mean a written note or mark, such as «a notation in the margin».
fact: In maths, notation includes symbols like +, ×, = and fractions.
fact: In music, notation is how notes are written on the stave.
fact: «Scientific notation» is a way to write very large or very small numbers using powers of ten.
exercise: «In maths, the + and × signs are part of the notation.» What does notation mean here? | A loud noise | A kind of food | A type of paper | *A system of signs or symbols used for writing
exercise: «In 3 × 4 = 12, which symbol shows multiply?» | *× | 12 | = | +
exercise: «Leo wrote a small notation next to his answer.» What is a notation in this sentence? | *A written note or mark | A large building | A long walk | A game played with cards
test: «Music uses notation to show which notes to play on the stave.» What is the notation in music? | *The written signs that show the notes | A type of instrument | A dance step | A loud sound
test: «Scientific notation helps us write very large numbers.» What is scientific notation used for? | *Writing very large or very small numbers | Running races | Cooking dinner | Painting pictures
exam: «The chess book explained the notation for each move, such as e4.» What does notation mean here? | A sports prize | *A system of signs used to record moves | A chess board | A type of piece
